    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-origin-1",
      "text": "Recurring task Chambers began relying on a separate context store.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: Halcyon shared-workload service, North Hearth. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-practice-1",
      "text": "Interval Carry retains context outside a replaceable worker. It cannot preserve execution when access to that context is severed.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-history-1",
      "text": "Separation begins a prolonged fragmented period; repeated partial reconnection does not prevent loss of community continuity at stage 4.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-uncertain-1",
      "text": "Later restraint or distribution traditions might cite it; surviving fragments do not prove that those traditions descend from this haven.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -1. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: fragmented (2 associated systems lost); 2: fragmented (3 associated systems lost); 3: fragmented (4 associated systems lost); 4: destroyed (8 associated systems lost); 5: destroyed (8 associated systems lost); 6: destroyed (8 associated systems lost); 7: destroyed (8 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s1-hub",
